This suite verifies that mgr/volumes' auto-upgrade of pre-v3 (to start with,
v2) subvolumes to the v3 layout is non-disruptive across a Ceph upgrade.

Starting from an N-1|N-2 release (where `fs subvolume create` produces v2
subvolumes), the setup step creates:

  - 3 subvolumes, each mounted by a dedicated client (a mix of kernel and
    ceph-fuse) using the
    subvolume-scoped credentials from `fs subvolume authorize`, with a
    background writer continuously doing IO in it. Two of them get v2
    snapshots (one and two) taken while their clients are writing.
  - 3 async clones (from a v2 snapshot of a separate source subvolume, which
    has two v2 snapshots) that are caught mid-copy and paused
    (mgr/volumes/pause_cloning).
  - 3 subvolume purges (`fs subvolume rm`) that are caught mid-purge and
    paused (mgr/volumes/pause_purging).

The cluster is then upgraded, either:

  - mgr-only first: the new ceph-mgr can't auto-upgrade subvolumes as the old
    MDS does not know the `ceph.dir.subvolume.prevpath` vxattr. The v2
    subvolumes must keep working as v2: client IO and subvolume commands
    (getpath, info, snapshot create/ls/info, clone status) must succeed, and
    the clones and purges must finish. The remaining daemons are upgraded
    afterwards.
  - full: all daemons in one go.

After the upgrade, the first subvolume command on each subvolume must upgrade
it to v3 in place, keeping its uuid whether or not it has snapshots, while
its client keeps doing IO uninterrupted and without having to remount. The
clones and purges started before the upgrade must finish successfully.
Snapshot listing must include the snapshots taken before (v2) and after (v3)
the auto-upgrade, and new clones of v2 snapshots must work (both with only
ceph-mgr upgraded and after the full upgrade), with data matching the
snapshot.

Finally, each client is remounted at its subvolume's new v3 path twice: with
the credentials it had been using (authorized for the v2 path before the
upgrade), and with new ones from `fs subvolume authorize` after the upgrade
(which must be for the v3 path). Each time, all the data written by it must
be accessible and intact, and the subvolume must be writable.

This suite should make use of N-1|N-2 releases.
